2 CONT b. circa 1355, d. 23 December 1392
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabella de Castilla was born circa 1355 at Morales, Spain.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the daughter of Pedro I, Rey de Castilla y León and Maria de Padilla.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Edmund of Langley, 1st Duke of York, son of Edward III, King of England and Philippe de Hainaut, between 1 March 1372 and 30 April 1372 at Hertford Castle, Hertford, Hertfordshire, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on 23 December 1392.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was also reported to have died on 3 November 1392.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was buried on 14 January 1392/93 at Church of the Dominicans, King's Langley, Hertfordshire, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabella de Castilla was invested as a Lady Companion, Order of the Garter (L.G.) in 1379.
