1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Constanza Sarmiento (d. after 1463). She was lady of Berganzo, Villaumbroso and Villatoquite and married Carlos Ramírez de Arellano, who was lord of the Cameros and was the son of Juan Ramírez de Arellano the Young
2 CONC er and Teresa Manrique, with whom she had several children. It is worth noting that in 1393 King Henry III confirmed to Constanza Sarmiento the grant of the 20 escusados, that is, exempt by privilege from paying taxes. Furthermore
2 CONC , her husband made a will on July 12, 1410 in the city of Antequera and died in 1412, leaving Constanza as guardian of their children, and she made a will in Andalusia on July 23, 1463, and was buried, like her husband, in the con
2 CONC vent of San Francisco de Soria.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leonor_Enr%C3%ADquez_de_Castilla
