1 NOTE {geni:about_me} It is known that the town belonged to the Pay Arias de Castro family from 1260, being known as "the towers of Pay Arias" until 1303, when Ferdinand IV gave it the Latin name “specula” meaning "watchtower", "lookout
2 CONC ", which so well reflects his position ̶ when he ratified his lordship and supported its repopulation, founding the town as such in 1307. Cupbearer to the queen, ambassador to the Papacy, mayor of Córdoba, lord of Castro el Viejo,
2 CONC  the powerful magnate Pay Arias de Castro was one of the main promoters of the feudal regime that spread throughout southern Córdoba in the Late Middle Ages. His initiative was also the strengthening of the defenses of Espejo to p
2 CONC rotect his lands, control the route of the Guadajoz River and garrison this sparsely populated countryside that marked the border with the Nasrid kingdom.
2 CONT
2 CONT The exact date of his death is unknown, but it would have occurred in the days before January 10, 1330, the date on which his son Ruy Páez de Castro endowed the chapel of San Martín, where he would be buried, in the cathedral chur
2 CONC ch of Córdoba.
