1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Richard le Despenser, 4th Baron Burghersh==
2 CONT '''Richard le Despenser, 4th Baron Burghersh, K.B (30 November 1396 – 7 October 1414)[1] was the son and heir''' of Thomas le Despenser, 1st Earl of Gloucester (1373–1400), by Constance of York.
2 CONT Constance was a daughter of Edmund of Langley, Duke of York, fourth surviving son of Edward III of England, and Isabella of Castile, a daughter of Peter of Castile. '''His ancestry and marriage placed him in influential circles of
2 CONC  the English nobility and he was appointed Knight, Order of the Bath, on 8 April 1413.'''[1]
2 CONT Life
2 CONT '''Richard married to his second cousin Lady Eleanor Neville'''[2] (a granddaughter of John of Gaunt, Duke of Lancaster (a brother of Edmund of Langley) and Katherine Swynford.[3]) '''He died when he was just 17, on 7 October 1414
2 CONC , without leaving issue.'''[4]
2 CONT '''His heir was his younger sister''' Isabel, who married successively Earl of Worcester, and then his cousin, Richard de Beauchamp, 13th Earl of Warwick. '''His widow Eleanor, Lady Burghersh remarried''' to Henry Percy, 2nd Earl 
2 CONC of Northumberland.
2 CONT Ancestry
2 CONT ....etc.
2 CONT From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Richard_le_Despenser,_4th_Baron_Burghersh
2 CONT
2 CONT _________________________
2 CONT ==Richard le Despenser1,2,3,4,5,6==
2 CONT Last Edited	2 Feb 2014
2 CONT '''M, #46031, b. 30 November 1396, d. before 16 April 1414'''
2 CONT '''Father'''	Sir Thomas le Despenser, 1st Earl Gloucester, 5th Lord Despenser, Constable of Gloucester & St. Briavel's Castle7,8,9 b. 22 Sep 1373, d. 16 Jan 1400
2 CONT '''Mother'''	Constance Plantagenet10,8,9 b. c 1374, d. 28 Nov 1416
2 CONT '''Richard le Despenser was born on 30 November 1396.10,1,4 He married Eleanor Neville''', daughter of Sir Ralph Neville, 1st Earl Westmoreland, 4th Baron Neville and Joan Beaufort, '''after 23 May 1412.'''7,1,2,3,4,5,6 '''Richard
2 CONC  le Despenser died before 16 April 1414 at Merton, Surrey, England; d.s.p.'''7,1,3,4,6
2 CONT '''Family	Eleanor Neville''' b. 1398, d. c 1473
2 CONT Citations
