2 CONT ==Richard le Despenser, 4th Lord Burghersh1 ==
2 CONT '''M, #107426, b. 30 November 1396, d. 7 October 1414'''
2 CONT Last Edited=22 Apr 2019
2 CONT Consanguinity Index=0.28%
2 CONT '''Richard le Despenser, 4th Lord Burghersh was born on 30 November 1396.2,3 He was the son''' of Thomas le Despenser, 1st and last Earl of Gloucester and Constance Langley.1,4 '''He married Lady Eleanor de Neville''', daughter of
2 CONC  Ralph de Neville, 1st Earl of Westmorland and Lady Joan de Beaufort, '''after 23 May 1412.5 He died on 7 October 1414 at age 17 at Merton, Surrey, EnglandG, without issue.1 He was buried at Tewkesbury, Gloucestershire, England'''
2 CONC G.1
2 CONT '''He succeeded as the 4th Lord Burghersh [E., 1330] in August 1409.1 He was appointed Knight, Order of the Bath (K.B.) on 8 April 1413.'''1
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT 1. [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Extin
2 CONC ct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume II, page 427. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT 2. [S11] Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Families: The Complete Genealogy (London, U.K.: The Bodley Head, 1999), page 109. Hereinafter cited as Britain's Royal Families.
2 CONT 3. [S8] BP1999 volume 1, page 17, says aged 14 in 1414. See link for full details for this source. Hereinafter cited as. [S8]
2 CONT 4. [S11] Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Families, page 110.
2 CONT 5. [S8] BP1999. [S8]
2 CONT From: https://www.thepeerage.com/p10743.htm#i107426
2 CONT
