2 CONT ____________________________
2 CONT Thomas le Despenser, 1st Earl of Gloucester KG (22 September 1373 – 13 January 1400) was the son of Edward le Despenser, 1st Baron le Despencer, whom he succeeded in 1375.
2 CONT A supporter of Richard II against Thomas of Woodstock and the Lords Appellant, he was rewarded with an Earldom as Earl of Gloucester in 1397.
2 CONT However, he supported Henry Bolingbroke on his return to England to become King Henry IV, only to be attainted (deprived of his Earldom because of a capital crime) for his role in the death of Thomas of Woodstock.
2 CONT He then took part in the Epiphany Rising, a rebellion led by a number of Barons aimed at restoring Richard to the throne by assassinating King Henry IV; this quickly failed when the conspirators were betrayed by Edward of Norwich,
2 CONC  2nd Duke of York to Henry. After fleeing to the western counties, a number of the Epiphany Rising conspirators were captured and killed by mobs of townspeople loyal to the king; Despenser was captured by a mob and beheaded at Bri
2 CONC stol on 13 January 1400.
2 CONT Thomas le Despenser married Constance, daughter of Edmund of Langley, 1st Duke of York. They had issue, of whom:
2 CONT * Elizabeth le Despenser (died young c. 1398)
2 CONT *''' Richard le Despenser, 4th Baron Burghersh (1396–1414)
2 CONT * Edward le Despenser (b. bef. 1400), died young
2 CONT * Hugh le Despenser (c. 1400–1401)
2 CONT * Isabel le Despenser (1400–1439), she married first Richard Beauchamp, 1st Earl of Worcester, she married second his cousin Richard de Beauchamp, 13th Earl of Warwick
2 CONT From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomas_le_Despenser,_1st_Earl_of_Gloucester 
