2 CONT Coat of arms of the House of Castro .
2 CONT For other people of the same name, see Isabel de Castro (disambiguation) .
2 CONT Isabel de Castro (d. after 1404). Galician lady of the House of Castro , she was the daughter of Alvar Pérez de Castro , Count of Arraiolos and Constable of Portugal , and María Ponce de León and great-great-granddaughter of King 
2 CONC Sancho IV of Castile .
2 CONT
2 CONT Family origins
2 CONT Daughter of Alvar Pérez de Castro , Count of Arraiolos and Constable of Portugal , and María Ponce de León. She was the paternal granddaughter of Pedro Fernández de Castro , Lord of Lemos and grandson of Sancho IV of Castile and t
2 CONC he Portuguese noblewoman Aldonza Lorenzo de Valladares . On her maternal side, her grandparents were Pedro Ponce de León "the Old" , Lord of Marchena and Bailén , and great-great-grandson of King Alfonso IX of León , and his wife 
2 CONC Beatriz de Jérica, great-granddaughter of Jaime I of Aragon .
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the sister of Beatriz de Castro and Ponce de León , who married Pedro de Lara , Count of Mayorga and great-great-grandson of Alfonso X the Wise , King of Castile and León.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage and offspring
2 CONT She married in 1385 1 with Pedro Enríquez de Castilla , Count of Trastámara and Constable of Castile and son of the infante Fadrique Alfonso of Castile and grandson of Alfonso XI the Justiciero , King of Castile and León . It is u
2 CONC nknown who were the legitimate or illegitimate children of Pedro Enríquez, although according to some authors, within the first group are the following: 2
2 CONT
2 CONT Fadrique Enríquez de Castilla (1388-1430). Duke of Arjona and Count of Trastámara . He married Aldonza de Mendoza , half-sister of the Marquis of Santillana . He was buried in the monastery of Santa Clara la Real in Toledo.
2 CONT Beatriz Enríquez de Castilla (1398-1455). Her first marriage was with Diego López Dávalos and later with Pedro Álvarez Osorio , lord of Cabrera and Ribera and count of Lemos . She was buried next to her husband in the monastery of
2 CONC  San Francisco in Villafranca del Bierzo .
2 CONT Some authors point out that the following children of Pedro Enríquez, whose existence is documented, were illegitimate:
2 CONT
2 CONT Enrique Enríquez. He received the towns of Viana de Robreda and El Bollo from his father. He married Leonor Álvarez de Robleda, lady of Veigas de Camba , and was the father of Pedro Enríquez , bishop of Mondoñedo between 1426 and 
2 CONC 1445.
2 CONT Constanza Enriquez de Castro (d. 1427). She married Pedro Diaz de Cadórniga.
2 CONT Alvar Perez de Castro.
2 CONT Fernando Enríquez. He was lieutenant of the castle of Allariz and accompanied his brother Fadrique on his campaigns in Andalusia.
2 CONT Leonor de Castro. She married Juan de Novoa and for the second time García Díaz de Cadórniga.
2 CONT Alonso Enriquez.
2 CONT Juan Enriquez.
2 CONT Luis Enriquez.
2 CONT Isabel Enriquez.
2 CONT Joanna Enriquez.
2 CONT References
2 CONT "Foundation for Medieval Genealogy" . 2000 . Retrieved 11 November 2009 .
2 CONT Pardo de Guevara and Valdés, 2000 , pp. 246-250.
2 CONT Literature
