1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Dicen fue amante de Fernando el Católico 
2 CONT aragon reyes católicos.
2 CONT
2 CONT The following pedigree information is for the benefit of the Torres Family Tree:
2 CONT
2 CONT You (meanining the grand children of Jose Barreras Torres)→ Philip Christopher Torgerson Torres (your father) → Jose Barreras Torres (his father) → Jose Epifanio Chavez Torres (his father) → Prajedes Apodaca Torres (his father) → 
2 CONC Maria Toribia Perfecta Torres (his mother) → Jose Francisco Apodaca (her father) → José Apodaca (his father) → Jose Felipe de Apodaca (his father) → Francisca Lucero de Godoy (his mother) → Nicolás Lucero de Godoy (her father) → S
2 CONC argento Major Juan Antonio Lucero de Godoy (his father) → Doña Francisca Gómez y Robledo (his mother) → Francisco Gomez de Vicente (her father) → Manuel Gómez de Portugal y López de Nava (his father) → Capt. Juan Gomez De Portugal
2 CONC  (his father) → Luís Avis de Portugal, 5° duque de Beja (his father) → Maria de Castela e Aragão, rainha consorte de Portugal (his mother) → Ferdinand II the Catholic, King of Aragon (her father) → Luisa De Estrada (his partner)
2 CONT
2 CONT From the above pedigree the Torres family tree selects to follow the descendants of Luisa and record a marvelous family De Estrada branch to include her grand- daughter Beatris de Estrada who emigrated Spain with her family at a v
2 CONC ery young age of 7. Later in the new world she would meet and marry the well recorded explorer Francisco Vasquez de Coronado y Lujan.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note- worthy is that Ferdinand II, the Catholic King of Aragon(partner to Luisa De Estrada and father of Alfonso de Estrada) together with his wife Isabel I were responsible for the original voyage and explorations of Cristobal Co
2 CONC lon, or Christopher Columbus in 1492 which led to the complete domination of Spain over the subsequent land acquisitions by Spain in the New World or Nueva Espana.
2 CONT
2 CONT Also from this pedigree the Torres Family Tree selects to follow the Ancestors of Beatris to include Grimaldo on the de Estrada branch and the Ha Nasi ancestors dating well into the turn of the first century. 
