1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Sir Thomas Blount I, Knight=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Sir Thomas Blount was a member of the aristocracy in England.
2 CONT * Thomas Blount was born in 1383 at Rock, Cornwall, England. He was the second (or third) son of Sir Walter Blount and his wife Sancha de Toledo de Ayala, and his eventual heir. Intended for the church, after the death without mal
2 CONC e issue of his brother Sir John Blount in1418 he in turn assumed the Lancastrian livery, and rose high in royal service to be made treasurer of Normandy
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Ben M. Angel notes:=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Birth dates given include 1371, 1378, and 1390. But Complete Peerage seems to imply that he hadn't reached the age of 14 by 1397. From that, I'd discount the two earlier suggested birth dates.
2 CONT
2 CONT * He was heir to his eldest brother John, who died in 1418. After this, he left his clerical career and entered a military career that culminated in serving as Sheriff of Derbyshire in 1446-1447. He died in 1456, according to Comp
2 CONC lete Peerage.
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id= 6000000225922667821&size=large}}  
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Unknown contributor: Sorry to tell this but Thomas WAS NEVER father of Sheriff Humphrey or any Humphrey . Humphrey WAS son of John and Alice (de la Bere) Blount.      Source: Weis "Ancestral Roots"  seventh Edition and Visitation 
2 CONC of Shropshire 1623 [corrected Visitation date]
2 CONT
2 CONT Humphrey's 6th great grandfather was King John of England   by Edwin Poor
2 CONT
2 CONT "Sir Thomas Blount, Treasurer of Normandy, d. 1456." --Magna Charta Sureties
2 CONT *__________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT "THOMAS BLOUNT, 3rd son and heir in 1418 to his elder brother John. 
2 CONT *He was intended to be a cleric, and in 1397 a Papal indult was obtained enabling him to hold a benefice as soon as he should reach the age of 14. 
2 CONT *By the settlement of 1413 he was allowed the manor of Edlaston, with the advowson of the church, until he should obtain a benefice. 
2 CONT *On succeeding his brother in the estates in 1418 he renounced a clerical career. 
2 CONT *He was a commissioner of array in Derbyshire in 1419, 
2 CONT *a Knight of the Shire in 1420, 
2 CONT *and J.P. from 1422 onwards. 
2 CONT *He was engaged in the French war from 1423 in the retinue of the Duke of Bedford, and 
2 CONT *commissioner for co. Leicester for a loan in 1426 and 1428. 
2 CONT *In 1426 he had a Papal indult for mass to be celebrated before daybreak. 
2 CONT *He was Treasurer of Normandy in 1429 and 1431; 
2 CONT *a commissioner to raise money in 1436 and later, and 
2 CONT *Sheriff of Derbyshire 1446-47. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, 1stly, Margaret, daughter of Thomas GRESLEY. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, 2ndly, Elizabeth, whose parentage is not known. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in 1456." 
2 CONT
2 CONT --Complete Peerage IX:333-4, (transcribed by Dave Utzinger)
2 CONT *_______________________
2 CONT
2 CONT The Marbury Ancestry by Meredith Bright Colket (The Magee Press, Philadelphia, 1936)
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Thomas Blount. b. aft 1371 of Elwaston, Derbyshire ENG. d. in 1456.
2 CONT
2 CONT Treasurer of Normandy 1412, 1437 and 1453. He married more than once, his first wife Margaret Gresley was the mother of Thomas.
2 CONT *________________________
2 CONT *'''Thomas Blount1 
2 CONT *'''M, #211929, b. 1390, d. 1456
2 CONT *Last Edited=18 Nov 2008
2 CONT *'''     Thomas Blount was born in 1390 at Rock, Cornwall, England.1 He was the son of Sir Walter Blount and Sancha de Ayala.1 He married Margaret Gresley, daughter of Thomas Gresley and Margaret Walsh.1 He died in 1456.1
2 CONT *'''Children of Thomas Blount and Margaret Gresley
