1 OCCU mayor of Castilla, mayor of Seville, corregidor of Jerez de la Frontera,
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Juan Arias de Saavedra "the Famous" (c. 1400-1458) was a Castilian nobleman, military man and civil servant of the House of Saavedra, first lord of El Viso and Castellar. He held the positions of chief magistrate o
2 CONC f Castile, mayor of Seville, and magistrate of Jerez de la Frontera, among others. He is sometimes confused with his namesake grandson, the first holder of the County of Castellar. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The exact place of his birth is unknown, being the son of Fernán Arias de Saavedra "the Good", warden of the Castle of Cañete and frontiersman of the wars of Granada, and Leonor Martel de Peraza, sister of Hernán Peraza Martel "th
2 CONC e Old", titled king of the Canary Islands. His older brother, namesake of his father, died without descendants fighting against the Moors at Setenil, leaving John as his father's successor. His only surviving brother was the famou
2 CONC s Marshal of Castile Gonzalo Arias de Saavedra, I Lord of Zahara, and advisor to Henry IV, who accompanied him in the conquest of Castellar and exercised the leadership of his house during the minority of his son Fernando. 
2 CONT
2 CONT His birth as a member of the House of Saavedra determined his participation in the Granada Wars, in which his father, grandfather and great-grandfather played an important role in military leadership. He was also a relative, on hi
2 CONC s mother's side, of Constable Álvaro de Luna, to whose side he belonged since his youth.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Juana de Avellaneda, daughter of Juan Álvarez de Avellaneda, lord of Castrillo and major ensign of Juan II, and Constanza Fajardo y Quesada, with whom he had seven children:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Juan Arias de Saavedra, II lord of El Viso. He died his father without offspring.[ 5]
2 CONT # Fernando Arias de Saavedra (1440-1496), III lord of El Viso and II lord of Castellar, mayor alfaqueque of Castile. He married Constanza Ponce de León (half-sister of the 1st Duke of Cadiz), natural daughter of Juan Ponce de León
2 CONC , 1st Marquis of Cadiz, and Catalina González de Oviedo. They were parents of three children, the eldest being Juan Arias de Saavedra, 1st Count of Castellar. He had second nuptials with Juana Ortiz de Guzmán (without offspring), 
2 CONC and third with Leonor de Esquivel (with whom he had two other children).[ 5]
2 CONT # Juana Arias de Avellaneda (1435). She married Diego de Cervantes and Álvarez de Toledo, Commander of the Order of Santiago.[ 10] They were parents of Diego de Cervantes Saavedra (father of Commander Leonel de Cervantes),[11] and
2 CONC  Gonzalo de Cervantes Saavedra (progenitor of the Casa de Cervantes in New Spain).[ 12]
2 CONT # Leonor Arias de Saavedra.[ 11]
2 CONT # Catalina Arias de Saavedra.[ 11]
2 CONT # Maria Arias Saavedra.[ 6]
2 CONT # Another daughter whose name is unknown married to the "chinter Ordiales, who died in the battle of Valdecartama". Without offspring.[ 11
2 CONT
2 CONT https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Juan_Arias_de_Saavedra
