2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Humphrey Audley was born after 1430. He was the son of James Tuchet, 5th Lord Audley (of Heleigh) and Eleanor de Holland.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on 4 May 1471 at Tewkesbury, Gloucestershire, England, killed in action.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT He fought in the Battle of Tewkesbury on 4 May 1471.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT An ancestor of the Audley family of Norfolk.[1]
2 CONT
