1 NOTE RECORDS:  THE COMPLETE PEERAGE  942.D24 VOL 3 P. 260.-1, VOL II P.
2 CONT 399-402. He joined his father-in-law, the Earl of Warwick and
2 CONT Salisbury, in the rebellion against the King(his brother) in favour of the
2 CONT deposed King, Henry VI, but, changing sides, assisted in King Edward's victory
2 CONT at Barnet, 14 Apr. 1471.  In this battle his wife's father was slain,
2 CONT whereupon he, "in consideration of that his marriage," was, by
2 CONT separater patents, each dat. 25 Mar. 1471/2, cr. Earl of Warwick and Earl of
2 CONT Salisbury.  On 20 May following he was made Great Chamberlain of
2 CONT England.
2 CONT He took part with the King in his expedition against France, 1474-75,
2 CONT at Calais, After the death of his wife he proposed to marry Mary, da. of
2 CONT the Duke of Burgundy, a match which was much opposed by the Queen Consort.
2 CONT  He was accused of high treason, found guilty, and attainted, 8 Feb
2 CONT 1477/8, whereby all his honours became forfeited.  He was executed in the
2 CONT Tower of London 18 Feb. following(said to have been drowned in a butt of
2 CONT malmsey).
