2 CONT ## ''[40]''.  Fernández Duro, 1891, p. 547. (Heraldist Faustino Menéndez Pidal de Navascués stated in his Spanish medieval Heraldic work: the Royal House of León and Castile that the wife of Fernando Alfonso de Valencia, was the d
2 CONC aughter of Alfonso IV (of Portugal), although he did not mention his name. Cfr. Menéndez Pidal de Navascués (1982), p. 122. And the prestigious medievalist Salvador de Moxó, based on what Salazar and Castro were consigned in the 1
2 CONC 7th century, pointed out that Fernando Alfonso married a "dama of the Portuguese royal house," although he did not mention his filiation or, as in the previous case, his name. Cfr. Moxó et al (1969), p. 182.)
2 CONT ## ''[33]''.  Salazar y Acha, 2021, p. 354. ((2021). Royal Academy of History and State Agency Official Gazette of the State, ed. The Real Dynasties of Spain in the Middle Ages (1st edition). Madrid: National Print of the State Ag
