2 CONT I can only deduce that this person was of great value in advising the Royals of Iberian Peninsula who had just taken charge of the lands and people of modern day northern New Mexico. Hostile or friendly, this had to be a heart bre
2 CONC aking experience for this ancestor and I am deeply depressed when I read all the follow-action throughout the 17th century. I can well understand that the up rising of 1680-92 was the last gasp of the native people to try to hold 
2 CONC on desperately to their homeland and culture.   So while I do share pride in the development of New Mexico and the entire Rio Ariba and Abajo regions, my heart still aches for those who were trampled upon to achieve this "progress
2 CONC ".
