1 NOTE OR "JUANA""OF CASTILLE"; QUEEN OF SPAIN 1504-1555
1 NOTE Also known as, La Loca.
2 CONT Queen Juana I Queen of Castile, Leon, Granada, Toledo, Galicia, Sevilla, Cordova, Mucia, Jaen, the Algarves, Algenciras, Gilbaltar, the canary islands, The Indias (Florida, Louisiana, California, Arizona, Nevada, Mexico, Argentina
2 CONC , Equador, Columbia, Puerto Rico, Cuba, Hispanola, Haiti, etc.), the Islands and the mainland of the ocean sea, Countess of Barcelona, Roussillon, and Cerdague, Lady of Biscay and Molina, Duchess of Athens and Neopatria, Margravin
2 CONC e of Oristano and Gocian. (Whew!
2 CONT Spain had become a world power alright.)
2 CONT Juana ascended Isabel I's throne in 1505 and that of her father, Ferdinando in 1516. Her father nominated her heir of all his Kingdom with her son, Carlos I as regent. This was done probably because of her mental instability which
2 CONC  is why she is known as Juana La Loca. Her husband Felipe I was king and regent from 1504 to 1506. And her son Calos I became king in 1516.
