1 NOTE ES.41168.SNAHN/1.1.2.3.1//OSUNA,C.141,D.71-116
2 CONT Documento 87: Escritura otorgada por Juana Ponce de Leon, mujer de Pedro de Porras, a favor de Rodrigo Ponce de León, III conde de Arcos, y de su sobrino Juan Ponce de Leon, hijo de Lope Ponce y Catalina de Petra, por la que les c
2 CONC ede todo el derecho que pudiese tener a varios donadios y casas en el termino de Utrera (Sevilla). Original. Logrono, 1487, mayo, 20.
2 CONT Documentos 99 al 101: Escrituras referentes al pleito seguido entre Rodrigo Ponce de Leon, III conde de Arcos, y su sobrino Juan Ponce contra Beatriz Ponce de Leon y su marido Diego Maldonado por la posesion de ciertas casas y don
2 CONC adíos en Utrera. Originales. Marchena, 1486, julio, 23 - noviembre, 13.  Research Copyright 2008, John J. Browne Ayes, All Rights Reserved, National and International.
1 NOTE Juan Ponce de Leon. Ponce began his career by serving as a page and squire for Pedro Nunez de Guzman the grand master of the Order of Calatrava. The legend surrounding Ponce imply that Ponce was of a humble birth, others say he ca
2 CONC me from an impoverished family that were nobles. The truth is this, if one is going to serve the grand master of the Calatrava one had to have been coming from a well entitled family. In any case, Ponce accompanied Pedro Nunez de 
2 CONC Guzman in the battle to reconquer Granada from the Moors as his page and Squire. It then would be logical to surmise that he gained his first taste of battle there and learned his logistics at Granada. In the early part of the 150
2 CONC 0's he went to Hispanola and destroyed the Taino and subjugated them. He was rewarded with a governorship at Higuey. His career next took him to Puerto Rico and in 1509 created a settlement there. He became governor of Puerto Rico
2 CONC  by royal decree. In the year of 1513 he traveled to what was to become La Florida. The gulf stream was discovered during that time. In 1521 he returned to La Florida and landed in the area around Caloosa Hatchee river. After a ti
2 CONC me the party was attacked by members of the Calusa tribe. During the battle Ponce took an arrow that had been laced with poison. He died of his wound in Havana. His grandson, Juan Troche de Leon transfered his remains to Puerto Ri
2 CONC co and interred him in San Juan de Puerto Rico.
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT Charles W. Arnade, "Tequesta", pp 1, 38
2 CONT Tio Aurelio, Fundacion de San German, San Juan 1956-pp 274
2 CONT Tio Aurelio, Nuevas Fuentes Para la Historia de Puerto Rico, San German, Puerto Rico, pp 653 1961
2 CONT Padre Murga Sanz, Vicente, Juan Ponce de Leon, 1959, pp 385
2 CONT http://digitalcollections.fiu.edu/tequestafiles/1967/67_1_04.pdf
2 CONT The Catholic Encyclopeadia.
2 CONT It seems I've found the source that informed me about how Spanish blood got mixed in with that of the Taino. For a time the Spaniards were allowed to marry Taino women, there was a royal decree issued by the crown that gave the Sp
2 CONC aniards the permission. So, others would have us believe that the resultant descendants of Los Indios y Espanoles were illigitimate. This new document discovered by me legitimizes all descendants of the latter in Puerto Rico.
2 CONT Source for new notes:
2 CONT  Título de la unidad: "Licencia de matrimonio con indias"
2 CONT   Archivo: Archivo General de Indias
2 CONT   Signatura: INDIFERENTE,419,L.5,F.270V-271R
2 CONT    Codigo de Referencia:
2 CONT   ES.41091.AGI/16403.15.413//INDIFERENTE,419,L.5,F.270V-271R
2 CONT   Titulo Nombre atribuido:
2 CONT   Licencia de matrimonio con indias
2 CONT   Fecha Creacion:
2 CONT   1514-09-27, (Valladolid)  -
2 CONT Historia Archivistica:
2 CONT   Signatura antigua: INDIFERENTE,419,L.5,F.37v-38r
2 CONT   Signatura Historico:
2 CONT   INDIFERENTE,419,L.5,F.37V-38R
2 CONT  Real Cedula a Don Diego Colon y a los jueces de la Isla Espanola, dando
2 CONT   licencia a cualquier persona natural de los reinos de Castilla, residente en
2 CONT   la isla, para que puedan casarse con indias naturales de aquella, porque
2 CONT   parece que esto redundara en beneficio de la poblacion de dicha isla.
2 CONT   Nota al margen: 'No fue en este despacho y aun no se ha hecho por Carta
2 CONT   patente'. Nota al pie: 'Hasta aqui llega el despacho que llevo Juan Ponce de
2 CONT   Leon'
2 CONT AREA DE CONDICIONES DE ACCESO Y UTILIZACION
2 CONT   Indices de Descripcion:
2 CONT   Almirante de las Indias
2 CONT   Colon, Diego
2 CONT   Isla de Santo Domingo
2 CONT   Licencias de matrimonio
2 CONT   Matrimonios con indios
2 CONT   Ponce de Leon, Juan
2 CONT   Valladolid (Valladolid)
2 CONT   Foliacion antigua: 37v-38r;
2 CONT
2 CONT "Miriam, John,
2 CONT Perhaps this might be of interest-- David Cuesta Camacho & Adolfo Perez Comas have published an article in the recent issue of Hereditas 2007 v.8 no. 2, p.37-105, "Juan Ponce de Leon el Adelantado, Su entorno familiar y algunas pr
2 CONC oyecciones familiares en PR." They are working on her origins, and they think that they were related, since both came from the same place, Santervas de Campos, secondly, because they married as soon as she got to Hispanola, and th
2 CONC irdly, at that time there were so few people that those of noble lineage preferred to marry among themselves. [p.39]
2 CONT They do mention both the Murga Sanz and the Devereux books, along with many documents from the Archivo General de Indias, Libros parroquiales and other sources.
2 CONT Saludos, "
2 CONT Ellen
2 CONT Special Note: Be it known that I haven't read the above article published in Puerto Rico, "Hereditas." The research I have done is 100 percent my own. I have browsed the Ministry of Culture, Spain and have gathered up documents as
2 CONC  well as family trees of my ancestors. Someday soon, I will work on the Ponce de Leon of Puerto Rico to compile a complete family tree that starts with my 36th Great Grandfather, Poncio de Minerva down into Puerto Rico itself.
2 CONT All Research contained within this entire family tree is Copyright 2008, John J. Browne Ayes, All Rights Reserved, National and International.
