1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ====Sir Thomas Blount, II, Knight
2 CONT * '''From:''' ''A Genealogical History of the Dormant: Abeyant, Forfeited, and Extinct Peerages of the British Empire''. Volume 3 By John Burke. [http://books.google.com/booksid=qf4GAAAAQAAJ&pg=PA167&lpg=PA167&dq=Thomas+Blount+Cat
2 CONC herine+Clifton&source=bl&ots=3q__FInGG&sig=6syNv3iYnxRudmoiiTWQzNjFvk&hl=en&ei=UR55TvmoGuTWiALlmcXYDw&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=5&ved=0CDsQ6AEwBDgo#v=onepage&q=Thomas%20Blount%20Catherine%20Clifton&f=false/ '''Pg. 167''
2 CONC ']:—
2 CONT
2 CONT * In 1462, King Edward IV granted him the manor of Milton Ross, & other estates in Leicester and Lincoln, and appointed him, in the same year, treasurer of Calais.  
2 CONT * He '''married first Agnes''', 
2 CONT ** D/O and heir of Sir John Hawley, KNT. of Canons, Utterby, in Lincolnshire. 
2 CONT *   SIR THOMAS BLOUNT, treasurer of Normandy, who was then seated at Elwaston, in Derbyshire, and to whom the Duke of Exeter gave one thousand marks (L666. 6s. 8d.) to found a charity at Leicester. Sir Thomas m. first, Margaret, d
2 CONC aughter of Sir Thomas Greseley, knt. of Greseley, in the county of Derby, and dying in 1456, left two sons and three daughters, viz.
2 CONT ** I. WALTER (Sir), lord high treasurer of England, created, in 1464, by patent, BARON MONTJOY, a dignity which expired with his descendant, Charles Blount, Earl of Devonshire, in 1606. (See BURKE'S Extinct and Dormant Peerage.)
2 CONT ** '''II. THOMAS (Sir), of whom presently.
2 CONT *   Upon the extinction of the Lords Mountjoy, the representation of the family devolved upon the descendant of the second son, the above named
2 CONT * '''SIR THOMAS BLOUNT: preceed we therefore with his line. In 1462, King EDWARD IV. granted him the manor of Milton Ross, and other estates in the counties of Leicester and Lincoln, and appointed him, in the same year, treasurer 
2 CONC of Calais. 
2 CONT ** '''He married first, Agnes''',
2 CONT *** '''daughter and heir of''' Sir John Hawley, knt. of Canons Utterby, in Lincolnshire, and '''had issue''',
2 CONT ** I. ROBERT, born in 1459, who died in 1514.
2 CONT ** II. Elizabeth, m. to Richard Hausard.
2 CONT * '''Sir Thomas espoused, secondly, Catharine, 
2 CONT *** daughter of Sir Gervase Clifton, of Clifton, Notts. and left by that lady, at his decease, 8th EDWARD IV. 1468, an only son,
2 CONT ** RICHARD BLOUNT, who m. ELIZABETH, only daughter and heir of WILLIAM DE LA FORD, of Iver, in the county of Buckingham, by whom he acquired the estate in that place, and purchasing the manor of MAPLE DURHAM GURNEY, in the county 
2 CONC of Oxford, on the 1st February, 1489, fixed his permanent abode there. He served the office of sheriff for Bucks and Bedfordshire in the 18th HENRY VII. A.D. 1502. He d. on the 31st November, 1508 (buried at Iver, Bucks), leaving 
2 CONC one son and two daughters, viz. ____________________
2 CONT
2 CONT ====Sir Thomas Blount
2 CONT * M,
2 CONT * b. circa 1420, d. 1468
2 CONT * Father:  Sir Thomas Blount b. c 1378, d. 1456 
2 CONT * Mother:  Margaret de Gresley b. c 1392, d. a 1430 
2 CONT * Sir Thomas Blount was born circa 1420 at of Milton Ross, Hereford, England. 
2 CONT * He '''married Agnes Hawley''', daughter of Sir John Hawley and Margaret, circa 1453. 
2 CONT * Sir Thomas Blount''' married Catherine Clifton''', daughter of Sir Gervase Clifton, Treasurer of Calais and Alice Neville, circa 1466. 
2 CONT * Sir Thomas Blount died in 1468.
2 CONT * '''Family:''' Agnes Hawley b. c 1432 
2 CONT * '''Children:''' 
2 CONT ** Agnes Blount+ b. c 1456, d. 20 Nov 1537
2 CONT ** Elizabeth Blount b. c 1458
2 CONT ** Robert Blount b. c 1460, d. 1514
2 CONT ** Richard Blount+ b. c 1464, d. 30 Nov 1508
2 CONT
2 CONT ====Citation
2 CONT * 1. Magna Charta Sureties, 1215, 4th Ed., by F. L. Weis, p. 82; The Royal Descents of 500 Immigrants, by Gary Boyd Roberts, p. 350; Stemmata Robertson, p. 203.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From:''' [http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p516.htm#i15519 Our Royal Titled Noble and Commoner Ancestors]
2 CONT
