1 OCCU 1st baron of mountjoy, I Barón de Mountjoy
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Walter Blount, 1st Baron Mountjoy=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Walter Blount, 1st Baron Mountjoy KG (c. 1416 – 1 August 1474) was an English politician.
2 CONT * Walter Blount was born about 1416, the eldest son''' of Sir Thomas Blount (1378–1456) and Margery Gresley and '''grandson of''' Sir Walter Blount.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walter_Blount,_1st_Baron_Mountjoy Walter Blount I, by Wikipedia]
2 CONT
2 CONT He was made Steward of the High Peak in Derbyshire and became a bitter rival of the local Vernon and Longford families, replacing the Vernons in parliament as the near permanent Knight of the Shire (1446–1448, 1450–1468) for Derby
2 CONC shire. He succeeded his father''', Sir Thomas Blount, '''as Treasurer of Calais in 1460, becoming governor a year later as a reward for service rendered to King Edward IV at the Battle of Towton. Edward conferred on him in 1467 ri
2 CONC ch estates in Devon forfeited by the Earl of Devon; and in 1465 Blount was made lord high treasurer and created Baron Mountjoy. This creation is noteworthy as one of the earliest examples of a baronial title not being of a territo
2 CONC rial character; nor the title of a dignity already existing. '''Blount's great-grandfather''' had married Isolda, daughter and heiress of Sir Thomas de Mountjoy, and the title was probably chosen to commemorate this alliance.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He was made a Knight of the Garter in 1472.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''On his death on 1 August 1474 in Greyfriars, London his grandson''' Edward Blount, 2nd Baron Mountjoy '''inherited his title. His eldest son''' (and Edward's father) Sir William Blount '''had been killed at the Battle of Barnet
2 CONC  in 1471.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Mountjoy married firstly Helena Byron''', the daughter of Sir John Byron of Clayton, Lancashire,[2] '''by whom he had four sons and two daughters.
2 CONT *William Blount, eldest son and heir, who died in 1471 of wounds received at the Battle of Barnet.[2]
2 CONT *John Blount, 3rd Baron Mountjoy, second son.
2 CONT *James Blount, third son.
2 CONT *Edward Blount.
2 CONT *Anne Blount.
2 CONT *Elizabeth Blount.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''By November 1467 Mountjoy married secondly Anne (née Neville), widow''' of Humphrey Stafford, 1st Duke of Buckingham (d.1460), and daughter of Ralph Neville, 1st Earl of Westmorland.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT ______________
2 CONT *'''Sir Walter Blount, 1st Lord Mountjoy, Lord High Treasurer1,2,3,4,5,6,7
2 CONT *'''M, #48675, b. circa 1420, d. 1 August 1474
2 CONT *Father	Sir Thomas Blount, Sheriff of Derbyshire, Treasurer of Normandy8,4,7 b. c 1378, d. 1456
2 CONT *Mother	Margaret de Gresley8,4,7 b. c 1392, d. a 1430
2 CONT *'''     Sir Walter Blount, 1st Lord Mountjoy, Lord High Treasurer was born circa 1420 at of Appletree, Derbyshire, England.8,4,7 He married Ellen Byron''', daughter of Sir John Byron and Margaret Booth, '''circa 1442.9,2,5 Sir Wa
2 CONC lter Blount, 1st Lord Mountjoy, Lord High Treasurer married Anne II Neville''', daughter of Sir Ralph Neville, 1st Earl Westmoreland, 4th Baron Neville and Joan Beaufort, '''before 25 November 1467; No issue.9,1,3,4,6,7 Sir Walter
2 CONC  Blount, 1st Lord Mountjoy, Lord High Treasurer left a will on 8 July 1474.4,7 He died on 1 August 1474; Buried in the Chapel of the Apostles, Church of the Grey Friars, London.9,1,4,7 His estate was probated on 10 February 1475.4
2 CONC ,7
2 CONT *'''Family 1     Ellen Byron b. c 1416, d. b 1467
2 CONT *Children	
2 CONT **Sir William Blount, Sheriff of Nottinghamshire & Derbyshire+9,10,2,5 b. c 1443, d. 14 Apr 1471
2 CONT **Sir John Blount, 3rd Lord Mountjoy+ b. c 1450, d. 12 Oct 1485
2 CONT *'''Family 2     Anne II Neville d. 20 Sep 1480
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 674.
