3 NOTE Wikipedia comments on the origin of the Marquisate of Valdecazarna in Spain, which before being declared as such, was a lordship. From the marriage of Martín Vázquez de Quirós and Inés de Miranda y Ponce de León eight children wer
4 CONC e born, among them, the eldest son, Diego Fernández de Miranda, lord of Villanueva del Infantazgo and numerous places, married to Isabel de Quirós, and fifth grandfather of the first Marquis of Valdecarzana. On April 11, 1504, Die
4 CONC go Fernández de Miranda founded a mayorazgo in favour  of his son Lope Bernaldo de Miranda. One of the clauses of the mayorazgo was the obligation of the heirs of the mayorazgo to use the surname Miranda.
