1 NOTE {geni:about_me} RICHARD HADLEY.  He married LADY PHILLIPA AUDLEY about 1493, daughter of SIR AUDLEY and ELIZABETH COURTENAY.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of RICHARD HADLEY and LADY AUDLEY are:
2 CONT
2 CONT  i. JAMES HADLEY.
2 CONT
2 CONT  ii. WILLIAM HADLEY.
2 CONT
2 CONT  iii. JOHN HADLEY.
2 CONT
2 CONT  iv. GEORGE HADLEY.
2 CONT
2 CONT  v. HENRY HADLEY.
2 CONT
2 CONT  vi. JAMES HADLEY.
2 CONT
2 CONT  vii. JANE HADLEY.
2 CONT
2 CONT  viii. ANNE HADLEY. 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~summer/Hadley.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Research Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT Estimated birth date: "born about 1470" is based on their parents' marriage 1463/4 and Richardson listing Philippe third of their three daughters, assuming one child every 2 years, the daughters' birth years can be reasonably gues
2 CONC sed as 1465, 1467, and 1469 (Richardson lists sons and daughters separately; if their son John was born before Philippe, that pushes her birth year estimate to 1471). ~ Noland-165 13:42, 21 January 2018 (EST)
2 CONT
2 CONT "Their [Philippe & Richard's] great-granddaughter, Margaret Hadley, and her husband, Thomas Luttrell, received a dispensation to marry, due to their relationship in the 3rd and 4th degrees. Both husband and spouse were descended f
2 CONC rom Elizabeth Courtenay, the former by her 1st husband, Sir James Luttrell, and the latter by her 2nd husband, Sir Humphrey Audley. The dispensation was issued by the Cardinal of St. Angelo, Papal Penitentiary, at St. Peter's, on 
2 CONC 28 Nov 1558.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT I could not find an entry for her or her parents (Humphrey and Elizabeth) in Cawley's Medieval Lands (although I found the 1st Lord Audley) or in Darryl Lundy's database, thepeerage.com. ~ Noland-165 13:28, 21 January 2018 (EST)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Debrett Report
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.hadleysociety.com/home/hadley-history/english-history/debrett-report/
2 CONT
2 CONT >Alexander Hadley is the earliest generation described in the family history; he is believed to have been born in London in 1375, the son of Sir John Hadley, who was elected a member of Parliament in 1369 and was twice Lord Mayor 
2 CONC of London (1379 and 1393). Alexander married Lady Alice Durborough (who was descended from the Fitzurse family), and they settled at Hadley Williton (now known as Williton Hadley), Somerset in about 1400. They were the parents of 
2 CONC John Hadley, who married Joan, daughter of Richard Stowell. John and Joan were the parents of Richard Hadley, who married Lady Phillipa, daughter of Sir Humphrey Audley by his wife Elizabeth Courtney. Elizabeth Courtney was descen
2 CONC ded from King Edward III. Richard and Philippa’s son was Joshua Hadley (although on a separate chart he is more correctly called '''James'''). …
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
