1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==George Nevill, 4th Baron Bergavenny==
2 CONT '''George Neville, or Nevill, 4th and de jure 2nd Baron Bergavenny (c.1440 – 20 September 1492) was an English nobleman.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''George Neville was the son of Edward Neville, 3rd Baron Bergavenny and Elizabeth Beauchamp. He was knighted by Edward IV on 9 May 1471,[1] after fighting for the King at the Battle of Tewkesbury. He succeeded his father in 1476
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Neville married firstly, before 1 May 1471, Margaret Fenne (d. 28 September 1485), the daughter and heiress of Hugh Fenne, Treasurer of the Household to King Henry VI, Escheator of Norfolk & Suffolk, by whom he had six sons and
2 CONC  a daughter:[2][3]
2 CONT * George Neville, 5th Baron Bergavenny (c.1469–c.1535).[3]
2 CONT * John Neville.[4]
2 CONT * William Neville.[4]
2 CONT * Sir Edward Neville (1471–1538), who married, before 6 April 1529, Eleanor (née Windsor), widow of Ralph Scrope, 9th Baron Scrope (d. 17 September 1515), and daughter of Andrew Windsor, 1st Baron Windsor.[3] He was the ancestor o
2 CONC f George Washington through his granddaughter Catherine.[5]
2 CONT * Sir Thomas Neville (c.1484–1542), Speaker of the House of Commons, who married firstly Katherine Dacre, and secondly Elizabeth Bryce.[6]
2 CONT * Sir Richard Neville[6] (bef. 1485 – c.1515).
2 CONT * Elizabeth Neville, who married firstly Thomas Berkeley, esquire, of Avon, Hampshire, and secondly Richard Covert, esquire, of Slaugham, Sussex.[6]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He married secondly a wife named Elizabeth whose surname is unknown. She was the widow successively of Richard Naylor, Sir Robert Bassett, and John Stokker. There were no issue of his second marriage.[2][3]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Bergavenny was a captain in the English forces at Calais in 1490, and died in 1492.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/George_Nevill,_4th_Baron_Bergavenny
2 CONT
2 CONT ________________________
2 CONT *'''Sir George Neville, Lord Abergavenny1,2,3,4,5,6
2 CONT *'''M, #22275, b. circa 1440, d. 20 September 1492
2 CONT *Father     Sir Edward Neville, 1st Baron Abergavenny7,8,9 b. c 1412, d. 18 Oct 1476
2 CONT *Mother     Elizabeth Beauchamp7,8,9 b. 16 Sep 1415, d. 18 Jun 1448
2 CONT *'''     Sir George Neville, Lord Abergavenny was christened circa 1440 at Staindrop, Durham, England.8,5 He was born circa 1440 at Raby Castle, Durham, England; Age 36 in 1476.2,8,5 He married Margaret Fenne, daughter of Hugh Fen
2 CONC ne, Esq., Treasurer of the Household to King Henry VI, Escheator of Norfolk & Suffolk, circa 1466 at of Scoulton, Norfolk, England; They had 6 sons (Sir George, Lord Bergavenny; John; William; Sir Edward; Sir Thomas, Speaker of th
2 CONC e House of Commons; & Sir Richard) and 1 daughter (Elizabeth, wife of Thomas Berkeley, Esq., & of Richard Covert, Esq.).2,10,3,5,6 Sir George Neville, Lord Abergavenny married Elizabeth before 29 February 1488 at of London, Middle
2 CONC sex, England; She had been married 3 times before (Richard Naylor, Alderman of London; Sir Robert Bassett, Alderman, Sheriff & Lord Mayor of London; & John Stokker, Alderman of London). No issue from her marriage to Sir George Nev
2 CONC ille.2,10,4,5 Sir George Neville, Lord Abergavenny died on 20 September 1492; Buried at Lewes Priory, Sussex.10,5 His estate was probated in January 1496.10,5
2 CONT *'''Family 1      Margaret Fenne b. 1444, d. 28 Sep 1485
2 CONT *Children
2 CONT **Elizabeth Neville+11,3,5,6 b. c 1467, d. a 1500
2 CONT **Sir George Neville, Lord Abergavenny, Constable of Dover Castle, Warden of the Cinque Ports+12,10,5 b. c 1469
2 CONT **Sir Edward Neville, Constable of Leeds Castle, Justice of the Peace for Kent+10,5 b. c 1471, d. 9 Jan 1539
2 CONT *'''Family 2      Elizabeth 
