2 CONT the late Lord Montaigue, was yesterday morning, about 7 o'clock, beheaded
2 CONT in a corner of the Tower, in presence of so few people that until evening
2 CONT the truth was still doubted" Writing to Queen Mary of Hungary, 10 jun
2 CONT 1541,
2 CONT Chapuys speaks of her "very strange and lamentable execution," which
2 CONT took place "at the Tower in the presence of the Lord Mayor of London and
2 CONT about 150 persons more."  In the absence of the executioner in the North " a
2 CONT wretched and blundering youth was chosen, who literally hacked her
2 CONT head and shoulders to pieces in the most pitiful manner"  Lord Herbert of
2 CONT Cherbury relates that he was assured by a person of great quality that
2 CONT she refused to lay her head on the block, saying: "So should Traitors do,
2 CONT and I am none: neither did it serve that the Executioner told her it was
2 CONT the fashion; so turning her gray head every way, she bid him, if he would
2 CONT have her head, to get it as he could:  So that he was constrained to
2 CONT fetch it off slovenly"  (Life and Raigne of King Henry the Eighth, 1649, p.
2 CONT 468.)
