1 CONT    1. ^ York was a direct descendant of Edmund of Langley, 1st Duke of York, the fourth surviving son of Edward III; the House of Lancaster was descended from John of Gaunt, the third surviving son of Edward III, and as such had a
1 CONC  superior claim over the House of York. However, Richard Plantagenet's mother was Anne de Mortimer, the most senior descendant of Edward III's second surviving son, Lionel of Antwerp. Lionel had been the eldest son of Edward III t
1 CONC o leave a surviving line of descent; as such, by modern standards, his line had an indisputably superior claim over that of his younger brother, John of Gaunt. By contemporary standards, this was by no means so certain; nonetheles
1 CONC s, it allowed Richard and then Edward a good title to the throne.
1 CONT
