1 CONT Elizabeth Plantagenet was the daughter of Edward IV Plantagenet, King of England <p10164.htm> and Elizabeth Wydevill <p10165.htm>. She was born on 11 February 1466 at Westminster Palace, Westminster, London, England.1 She and Geor
1 CONC ge Neville, 1st and last Duke of Bedford <p1451.htm> were engaged.2 She married Henry VII Tudor, King of England, son of Sir Edmund Tudor, 1st Earl of Richmond <p10190.htm> and Margaret Beaufort <p10190.htm>, on 18 January 1486 at
1 CONC  Westminster Abbey, Westminster, London, England.1 She died on 11 February 1503 at age 37 at Tower of London, The City, London, England, childbirth.1 She was buried at Westminster Abbey, Westminster, London.1  She was also known a
1 CONC s Elizabeth of York.3 Through her marriage, Elizabeth Plantagenet gained the title of Queen Elizabeth of England on 18 January 1486. Through her marriage, Elizabeth Plantagenet gained the title of Queen Consort Elizabeth of Englan
1 CONC d on 25 November 1487.1
1 CONT Children of Elizabeth Plantagenet and Henry VII Tudor, King of England:
1 CONT Edward Tudor <p10497.htm> Arthur Tudor, Prince of Wales b. 20 Sep 1486, d. 2 Apr 1502 Lady Margaret Tudor <p10143.htm>+ b. 28 Nov 1489, d. 18 Oct 1541 Henry VIII Tudor, King of England <p10148.htm>+ b. 28 Jun 1491, d. 28 Jan 1547 
1 CONC Elizabeth Tudor <p10148.htm> b. 2 Jul 1492, d. 14 Sep 1495 Mary Rose Tudor <p10148.htm>+ b. 18 Mar 1496, d. 25 Jun 1533 Edmund Tudor, Duke of Somerset <p10148.htm> b. 21 Feb 1499, d. 19 Jun 1500 Katherine Tudor <p10148.htm> b. 2 F
1 CONC eb 1503, d. c 18 Feb 1503
